WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:52.377
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:52.647 --> 00:54.605
Oh, man.

3
00:54.605 --> 00:58.564
Lieutenant, we gotta hurry.

4
00:58.564 --> 01:02.355
Nothing I can do right now. The road is completely blocked.

5
01:02.355 --> 01:04.564
We really need an office at NOI.

6
01:04.564 --> 01:08.397
Can't believe we have to drive there for every meeting.

7
01:08.397 --> 01:12.023
They say we're part of NOI, but it's like we're invisible there.

8
01:12.023 --> 01:13.939
People bump into me every time I'm at NOI.

9
01:13.939 --> 01:16.064
It's worse than subway stations.

10
01:16.064 --> 01:19.064
Wait, are we literally invisible to them?

11
01:19.064 --> 01:23.023
Another thing, why are we even lumped together with Violent Crimes?

12
01:23.023 --> 01:26.731
Is it so hard to make a Traffic Crimes division?

13
01:26.731 --> 01:28.147
Captain,

14
01:28.147 --> 01:32.647
you gotta put your foot down and tell them to split us from Violent Crimes,

15
01:32.647 --> 01:34.522
and get us our own office too.

16
01:34.522 --> 01:35.939
Okay.

17
01:35.939 --> 01:38.564
We've crossed the Rubicon and casted the dice.

18
01:38.564 --> 01:41.023
[Cross the Rubicon - To cross the point of no return] I'm putting my foot down.

19
01:41.023 --> 01:44.023
[Cast the dice - Betting everything on the last line.] Good.

20
01:44.023 --> 01:45.981
And where the hell is the nerd?

21
01:45.981 --> 01:48.188
Lieutenant, did you hear?

22
01:48.188 --> 01:53.064
Investigator Cha went to the EOD training as an observer.

23
01:53.064 --> 01:56.889
[EOD: Explosive Ordinance Disposal]

24
02:05.355 --> 02:09.064
He went head-to-head with the Counter Terrorism unit.

25
02:09.064 --> 02:11.605
The opponent was a robot to boot.

26
02:11.605 --> 02:15.439
It was a robot match, then. Because Mr. Cha is practically a robot.

27
02:15.439 --> 02:18.139
Isn't that an overstatement?

28
02:37.147 --> 02:39.181
Oh my god!

29
02:47.856 --> 02:49.856
Human versus robot.

30
02:49.856 --> 02:53.847
And the human is one of us, the Traffic Crimes division.

31
02:55.064 --> 02:59.981
The sensor power cable is at the edge of the circuit. This is a fake.

32
02:59.981 --> 03:03.564
The real trigger is the contact circuit next to the elad switch.

33
04:27.772 --> 04:29.647
Investigator Cha beat the robot?

34
04:29.647 --> 04:33.439
Yes! The robot, defeated by a human who's practically a robot.

35
04:33.439 --> 04:35.397
That's crazy.

36
04:35.397 --> 04:37.188
Revenge of mankind!

37
04:37.188 --> 04:40.814
AI is no match for humans just yet!

38
04:40.814 --> 04:44.397
Dong Gi, how's that relevant?

39
04:44.397 --> 04:46.647
Where did you hear that anyway?

40
04:46.647 --> 04:50.314
Well, I have my sources.

41
04:50.314 --> 04:52.847
Do you want me to call him?

42
04:56.856 --> 04:59.223
Hey! Move!

43
05:16.314 --> 05:17.981
- Are you all right? - Oh my, I'm fine.

44
05:17.981 --> 05:19.314
I'm sorry.

45
05:24.105 --> 05:29.188
You are under arrest for traffic violation, reckless driving,

46
05:29.188 --> 05:31.355
and aggravated robbery.

47
05:31.355 --> 05:36.264
It's you again! Who are you, anyway?

48
05:38.397 --> 05:39.939
TCI.

49
05:39.939 --> 05:42.272
TCI?

50
05:42.272 --> 05:44.347
Is that a chicken joint?

51
05:49.355 --> 05:54.647
TCI. Traffic Crime Investigation.

52
05:59.605 --> 06:01.480
[Episode 1]

53
06:01.480 --> 06:04.480
- Why is he taking so long? - Should we go in without him?

54
06:04.480 --> 06:08.514
We are already late. A few minutes won't make a difference.

55
06:09.689 --> 06:12.105
- Oh. - I'm sorry.

56
06:12.105 --> 06:15.647
- I was held up- - By what? You met a robber or something?

57
06:15.647 --> 06:17.814
Just come. We are late.

58
06:17.814 --> 06:19.555
You are hopeless.

59
06:20.814 --> 06:23.105
According to the Prosecutors' Office,

60
06:23.105 --> 06:27.188
rejection rate for detention warrants reached 25%.

61
06:27.188 --> 06:29.680
Same for arrest warrants.

62
06:30.230 --> 06:32.480
These are not mere numbers.

63
06:32.480 --> 06:36.272
They point to declining trust toward our investigative efforts.

64
06:38.355 --> 06:41.105
People do not trust the police.

65
06:41.939 --> 06:44.355
What do you think is the cause?

66
06:46.272 --> 06:50.230
Well, the bottom line is,

67
06:50.230 --> 06:53.647
we lack specialized investigators.

68
06:53.647 --> 06:58.314
As seasoned veterans leave the force,

69
06:58.314 --> 07:01.772
inexperienced newcomers fill the void.

70
07:02.397 --> 07:06.188
Detectives are complaining about too much workload.

71
07:06.188 --> 07:09.897
Distrust toward us does not come from staff shortage.

72
07:09.897 --> 07:12.689
It is from the misconception that we are above than prosecutors.

73
07:12.689 --> 07:15.772
We have been given greater powers, while our system remains outdated.

74
07:15.772 --> 07:16.981
It is bound to cause issues.

75
07:16.981 --> 07:18.772
What do you mean, misconception?

76
07:18.772 --> 07:21.397
Are you saying it's our fault?

77
07:21.397 --> 07:23.355
Who are you blaming, exactly?

78
07:23.355 --> 07:26.272
I'm not blaming anyone. I'm merely stating the facts.

79
07:26.272 --> 07:29.522
People do not want the police to be above prosecutors.

80
07:29.522 --> 07:31.772
They want a government body to uphold justice.

81
07:31.772 --> 07:34.230
We need to clarify our identity first.

82
07:34.230 --> 07:36.647
Are we a policing body, or an investigative body?

83
07:36.647 --> 07:40.147
Identity sounds nice and all,

84
07:40.147 --> 07:43.856
but you're saying we should deliver indictment-ready investigations

85
07:43.856 --> 07:47.147
when we don't have enough manpower or resources?

86
07:47.147 --> 07:50.314
It is no longer about taking responsibilities.

87
07:50.314 --> 07:52.397
It's more like a punishment.

88
07:52.397 --> 07:55.856
- I didn't mean- - Stop.

89
07:56.522 --> 07:59.605
We are not here to point fingers.

90
07:59.605 --> 08:02.647
We have gathered here

91
08:02.647 --> 08:06.564
to find ways to win back people's trust.

92
08:10.605 --> 08:13.355
Opinions, anyone?

93
08:16.188 --> 08:18.105
It is too close…

94
08:18.772 --> 08:21.181
Captain Jung, from TCI?

95
08:25.230 --> 08:27.889
-Nothing. -Don't worry, feel free to share.

96
08:40.188 --> 08:44.223
Well, we need a space…

97
08:46.897 --> 08:48.314
What?

98
08:56.814 --> 08:58.480
We need a room, so…

99
09:00.272 --> 09:02.764
A room? What are you…

100
09:13.314 --> 09:16.897
I mean, an open chatroom,

101
09:16.897 --> 09:20.897
to share opinions.

102
09:25.439 --> 09:28.605
Okay. We'll consider it.

103
09:28.605 --> 09:32.355
No further comments? Then let's call it a day.

104
09:53.439 --> 09:54.939
Captain Jung?

105
09:54.939 --> 09:58.856
Chatroom? That's brilliant.

106
09:58.856 --> 10:01.897
You NOI guys are really something, huh?

107
10:01.897 --> 10:05.564
How about we open our own chatroom at Namgang Station, too?

108
10:05.564 --> 10:08.147
We might as well, sir.

109
10:09.105 --> 10:13.439
That was brilliant. You look stressed, though.

110
10:13.439 --> 10:16.814
Maybe you need a spa room instead of a chatroom.

111
10:16.814 --> 10:19.439
So that I can use it too.

112
10:19.439 --> 10:23.097
Bravo. You're the best. Keep up the good work.

113
10:27.731 --> 10:29.147
Yes?

114
10:36.230 --> 10:37.772
You have a request?

115
10:37.772 --> 10:41.147
I think you should return the TCI team to Namgang.

116
10:41.147 --> 10:43.272
It's affecting operation efficiency.

117
10:43.272 --> 10:46.272
What's more, it doesn't make sense.

118
10:46.272 --> 10:47.647
What does traffic investigation have to do with violent crimes?

119
10:47.647 --> 10:52.139
Not to mention organizational overlap and confusion in the chain of command.

120
10:53.814 --> 10:55.347
Efficiency, you say?

121
10:56.605 --> 11:00.355
Usually, when people use efficiency as a reason,

122
11:00.355 --> 11:01.772
they have something else in mind.

123
11:01.772 --> 11:05.597
I'm only concerned about our operations.

124
11:06.272 --> 11:09.731
Do you think TCI is affecting efficiency…

125
11:09.731 --> 11:12.764
because of Lieutenant Min?

126
11:14.105 --> 11:16.597
No, ma'am. You misunderstood.

127
11:18.314 --> 11:20.388
Glad to hear.

128
11:22.355 --> 11:25.230
TCI is not just a traffic unit.

129
11:25.230 --> 11:29.397
I believe they will prove essential in NOI operations,

130
11:29.397 --> 11:31.897
for both Detective Bureau and Investigation Bureau.

131
11:31.897 --> 11:36.388
Today, all violent crimes have elements of traffic crimes.

132
11:38.647 --> 11:40.188
Don't you think so?

133
11:43.314 --> 11:44.856
Let's give them some time.

134
11:44.856 --> 11:49.355
We'll discus the TCI issue with the new director.

135
11:53.314 --> 11:56.597
Anything else?

136
11:57.564 --> 11:59.388
No, ma'am.

137
12:14.355 --> 12:15.522
Just wait and see.

138
12:15.522 --> 12:19.647
Like I said, as part of NOI, we can pick our own cases.

139
12:19.647 --> 12:24.272
It means we can dig up those old unsolved cases.

140
12:24.272 --> 12:26.188
The illegal taxi case.

141
12:26.188 --> 12:27.856
We gotta see it through.

142
12:42.647 --> 12:46.105
Hey, Lieutenant!

143
12:46.105 --> 12:49.023
I told you not to park like this!

144
12:49.023 --> 12:52.188
Why? This is how I park!

145
12:52.188 --> 12:54.105
I'm not riding with you any more.

146
13:10.188 --> 13:12.147
When he said 'room,'

147
13:12.147 --> 13:15.147
I didn't think that room would be in the cyber space.

148
13:15.147 --> 13:19.397
I was a little excited, and now I'm ashamed.

149
13:19.397 --> 13:22.314
Captain, what happened to Rubicon?

150
13:22.314 --> 13:24.639
You said the dice was casted!

151
13:25.188 --> 13:26.647
According to Sun Tzu,

152
13:26.647 --> 13:28.605
one should know what battles to pick.

153
13:28.605 --> 13:31.355
[Pick your battles] You need to know when to advance and retreat.

154
13:31.355 --> 13:33.564
[Know when to advance or retreat] That's how you save yourself from ruin.

155
13:33.564 --> 13:36.397
Yeah, Sun Tzu would be so proud of you.

156
13:36.397 --> 13:37.397
And you know this saying?

157
13:37.397 --> 13:39.814
-"Keep your word." -You saw how it was.

158
13:39.814 --> 13:42.188
If I hadn't thought on my feet,

159
13:42.188 --> 13:44.605
we'd been buried alive.

160
13:44.605 --> 13:46.731
We already are.

161
13:46.731 --> 13:48.522
We don't even have a room at NOI.

162
13:48.522 --> 13:51.314
We work for NOI, but we are Namgang Station's TCI.

163
13:51.314 --> 13:53.897
We have to walk that direction, and the other direction.

164
13:53.897 --> 13:55.814
It's like we're in the intersection.

165
13:55.814 --> 13:57.731
No.

166
13:57.731 --> 14:00.314
We're in the complement, not intersection.

167
14:08.397 --> 14:09.897
We're not in the intersection.

168
14:09.897 --> 14:14.480
We're neither in A nor B. We could be here, or there.

169
14:15.897 --> 14:17.430
Thus, complement.

170
14:18.564 --> 14:21.188
Yeah, complement.

171
14:21.188 --> 14:23.605
Thanks for the clarification.

172
14:23.605 --> 14:28.439
If I had you as a teacher, I wouldn't have given up on math.

173
14:30.856 --> 14:32.480
Superintendent!

174
14:32.480 --> 14:34.314
- Ma'am. - How can I help you?

175
14:34.314 --> 14:35.397
A case.

176
14:35.397 --> 14:38.897
Chief, we just got back from NOI.

177
14:38.897 --> 14:40.480
Hey!

178
14:40.480 --> 14:42.772
You're here to work, right?

179
14:42.772 --> 14:46.564
This is not a hotel, you know.

180
14:46.564 --> 14:47.856
If you don't want to work, just leave.

181
14:47.856 --> 14:49.480
Ugh, who said I wasn't going to do it?

182
14:49.480 --> 14:52.814
Ever since you got pregnant, you've gotten awfully touchy.

183
14:52.814 --> 14:54.939
So don't get on my nerves.

184
14:54.939 --> 14:57.897
The hormones are really acting up.

185
14:57.897 --> 15:00.439
Well, you did the deed, so-

186
15:00.439 --> 15:02.564
I did the deed?

187
15:02.564 --> 15:05.272
He went full beast mode, like…

188
15:11.064 --> 15:14.564
You make me say the darndest things.

189
15:14.564 --> 15:18.181
Anyway, hang in there, guys.

190
15:18.772 --> 15:21.764
Take care, ma'am.

191
15:22.897 --> 15:25.439
Well, she's definitely off the promotion race.

192
15:25.439 --> 15:26.897
What a shame, she worked so hard.

193
15:26.897 --> 15:28.023
But the "beast" happened.

194
15:28.023 --> 15:31.064
- That's why I don't get married. - Don't, or can't?

195
15:31.064 --> 15:32.764
Sorry.

196
15:37.188 --> 15:40.856
[Naeguro 20-gil Automobile-bicycle crash]

197
15:40.856 --> 15:43.272
Crashed with a bicycle…

198
15:43.272 --> 15:46.397
[Two killed, one injured]

199
15:48.564 --> 15:51.397
[Driver alleges unintended acceleration]

200
16:23.689 --> 16:26.230
The driver was 36 years old, Han Soo In.

201
16:26.230 --> 16:28.981
She was driving her husband to work.

202
16:28.981 --> 16:30.814
She's in the hospital.

203
16:30.814 --> 16:34.314
Her husband had passed away when the rescue team arrived.

204
16:34.314 --> 16:35.856
What about the passenger seatbelt?

205
16:35.856 --> 16:40.064
According to the responders, he wasn't wearing a seatbelt.

206
16:40.064 --> 16:42.939
The passenger airbag didn't work, either.

207
16:42.939 --> 16:45.439
The driver airbag worked fine, though.

208
16:45.439 --> 16:49.856
The driver said something over and over.

209
16:49.856 --> 16:52.230
I didn't do it.

210
16:52.230 --> 16:54.856
The car moved by itself.

211
16:54.856 --> 16:57.689
The car went crazy.

212
16:57.689 --> 17:00.314
She claimed sudden acceleration?

213
17:00.314 --> 17:02.023
You can say that.

214
17:03.397 --> 17:07.147
Pedal dash cam… nope.

215
17:07.939 --> 17:10.647
Hey, what are you doing!

216
17:10.647 --> 17:12.772
Back up! Leave!

217
17:12.772 --> 17:16.064
Leave the area!

218
17:16.064 --> 17:17.105
You can't do that.

219
17:17.105 --> 17:20.439
I said leave.

220
17:23.731 --> 17:27.230
What's happening? No, no!

221
17:27.230 --> 17:28.772
Honey!

222
17:31.355 --> 17:35.064
Recording indicates sudden acceleration.

223
17:35.064 --> 17:36.856
That's what they all say.

224
17:36.856 --> 17:40.064
"The car went berserk. It went out of control."

225
17:40.064 --> 17:41.856
[EDR: Endpoint Detection and Response] But EDR shows

226
17:41.856 --> 17:46.272
[EDR: Endpoint Detection and Response] they mistook gas for brake in 99% of cases.

227
17:46.272 --> 17:49.647
Like the Gangnam Station crash.

228
17:49.647 --> 17:51.981
No sudden acceleration claim has been accepted in court.

229
17:51.981 --> 17:54.856
Right? It's so obvious.

230
17:54.856 --> 17:57.439
This crash claimed two lives,

231
17:57.439 --> 17:59.188
including her husband.

232
17:59.188 --> 18:01.397
Whatever the facts are,

233
18:01.397 --> 18:03.939
the driver is going through hell.

234
18:03.939 --> 18:07.480
So, let's not jump to conclusions until we get the forensic results.

235
18:07.480 --> 18:09.023
Right.

236
18:09.023 --> 18:13.230
Do they have children?

237
18:13.230 --> 18:14.272
No.

238
18:14.272 --> 18:17.689
The registration card says the husband is her only family.

239
18:17.689 --> 18:20.897
Passenger airbag had been manually disabled.

240
18:20.897 --> 18:25.105
It should have been enabled, unless they had a booster seat.

241
18:25.105 --> 18:28.388
Someone did this on purpose, expecting an accident?

242
18:29.689 --> 18:32.597
Now that you mention this, Dong Gi, run the clip again.

243
18:35.105 --> 18:37.272
What's happening? No, no!

244
18:37.272 --> 18:39.355
Honey!

245
18:42.272 --> 18:44.272
The husband was so quiet.

246
18:44.272 --> 18:46.105
Despite his wife's desperate cries.

247
18:46.105 --> 18:50.272
You're right. Even if he was asleep, in such a situation…

248
18:50.272 --> 18:53.064
The passenger did not wear the seatbelt, right?

249
18:53.064 --> 18:56.147
Could it be the wife?

250
18:56.147 --> 18:59.731
If the wife had planned it, she wouldn't have cried out like this.

251
18:59.731 --> 19:02.856
She was acting because she knows they have a dash cam.

252
19:02.856 --> 19:05.147
Don't get ahead of yourselves.

253
19:05.147 --> 19:06.564
One step at a time, okay?

254
19:06.564 --> 19:09.856
Sure, but we have to alert the insurance association, right?

255
19:09.856 --> 19:12.472
What's the husband's insurance?

256
19:12.981 --> 19:14.814
Why? Did I say something wrong?

257
19:14.814 --> 19:17.981
- Yeon Ho and So Hee, you- - Check on the driver, got it.

258
19:17.981 --> 19:19.605
Okay, then.

259
19:19.605 --> 19:22.689
- Hyun Kyung and Dong Gi, - We'll take statements.

260
19:24.480 --> 19:27.314
I'll contact NFS, then.

261
19:27.314 --> 19:29.439
Let's alert the insurance association first.

262
19:29.439 --> 19:32.097
Lieutenant told you not to get ahead.

263
19:32.814 --> 19:35.939
- Hey. - Sir.

264
19:36.981 --> 19:40.564
Your chief is here, and you guys start sitting down?

265
19:40.564 --> 19:43.522
Everything's backwards in here!

266
19:43.522 --> 19:46.188
Anyway, is that true?

267
19:46.188 --> 19:49.064
- What do you mean… - I mean, that case!

268
19:50.023 --> 19:52.856
About the father, is is true?

269
19:52.856 --> 19:55.188
Whose father, sir?

270
19:55.188 --> 19:57.856
Is "True" the father's name?

271
19:57.856 --> 19:59.981
You little…

272
19:59.981 --> 20:01.981
That's not even funny.

273
20:01.981 --> 20:06.564
Is the driver's father a judge?

274
20:06.564 --> 20:08.023
Is it true

275
20:08.023 --> 20:11.564
that the driver's father is a judge?

276
20:11.564 --> 20:13.181
- Huh? - Huh?

277
20:14.023 --> 20:16.105
What, you didn't know?

278
20:16.689 --> 20:18.731
This is Lieutenant Min, right?

279
20:18.731 --> 20:20.564
Judge's daughter claims sudden acceleration.

280
20:20.564 --> 20:21.689
"Nangam" Station…

281
20:21.689 --> 20:23.647
Can't believe they botched the spelling.

282
20:23.647 --> 20:25.272
It's just embarrassing.

283
20:25.272 --> 20:26.981
Are you okay with taking the case?

284
20:26.981 --> 20:29.772
I think you should let it go.

285
20:29.772 --> 20:32.731
We can't. It came to us.

286
20:32.731 --> 20:34.981
And we've gone metropolitan, you know.

287
20:34.981 --> 20:36.814
Metropolitan my butt.

288
20:36.814 --> 20:40.439
You play it wrong, and you'll get crushed from both sides.

289
20:40.439 --> 20:42.439
Which side are you gonna pick?

290
20:42.439 --> 20:43.897
What do you even mean?

291
20:43.897 --> 20:45.397
We have to uncover the truth-

292
20:45.397 --> 20:46.897
No, I mean,

293
20:46.897 --> 20:50.105
whose side is the truth on?

294
20:50.105 --> 20:52.647
Whether it's sudden acceleration or the driver's fault,

295
20:52.647 --> 20:54.439
no matter what it is,

296
20:54.439 --> 20:58.023
you guys will be in a pickle.

297
20:58.023 --> 21:00.272
Just think about it.

298
21:00.272 --> 21:04.647
Reporters will ask all sorts of questions, like whether there was political pressure.

299
21:04.647 --> 21:08.355
My head hurts just thinking about it.

300
21:08.355 --> 21:11.023
You are giving us pressure right now.

301
21:11.023 --> 21:12.647
Just let us do our job.

302
21:12.647 --> 21:14.439
I'm just worried.

303
21:14.439 --> 21:17.772
You guys gave me so much stress last year.

304
21:17.772 --> 21:20.188
Now I've got diabetes, hypertension-

305
21:20.188 --> 21:22.605
- Drinking gives you diabetes, Hyun Kyung. - Correct.

306
21:22.605 --> 21:25.023
Don't you say weird things.

307
21:25.023 --> 21:28.772
Did you dye your hair?

308
21:28.772 --> 21:31.023
No, but I'm going to.

309
21:31.023 --> 21:34.981
So you're considering it?

310
21:34.981 --> 21:37.897
Yeon Ho, you're wearing glasses again?

311
21:38.731 --> 21:39.939
I had a haircut.

312
21:39.939 --> 21:41.564
He lost weight.

313
21:41.564 --> 21:43.147
She got a glowup.

314
21:43.147 --> 21:45.564
That's just a lie. You guys heard him right?

315
21:45.564 --> 21:46.647
Investigate this properly!

316
21:46.647 --> 21:50.137
- Yes, sir! - I'm not finished!

317
21:50.731 --> 21:52.856
I dyed my hair, too!

318
21:52.856 --> 21:55.023
You didn't notice? Why is nobody concerned?

319
21:55.023 --> 21:56.564
I said I dyed my hair, too!

320
22:06.314 --> 22:08.264
Is he… gone?

321
22:11.564 --> 22:13.264
Both of them?

322
22:22.772 --> 22:24.931
Can I help you?

323
22:25.605 --> 22:27.439
We're the police.

324
22:27.439 --> 22:31.564
I need to ask Ms. Han a few things about the accident.

325
22:31.564 --> 22:34.314
- She is… - It's okay, Mom.

326
22:35.230 --> 22:37.188
Can you get me some fruit?

327
22:37.188 --> 22:39.814
- There's some here… - I want something else.

328
22:51.439 --> 22:55.023
Go on, ask your questions.

329
22:55.023 --> 22:56.314
How are you feeling?

330
22:56.314 --> 22:57.981
I'm fine.

331
22:58.564 --> 23:03.230
But my parents insisted that I stay in the hospital.

332
23:04.272 --> 23:07.105
You mentioned it was sudden acceleration?

333
23:07.105 --> 23:10.597
Could you please share what happened?

334
23:17.023 --> 23:19.981
Nothing was out of ordinary that morning.

335
23:19.981 --> 23:24.647
I usually drive my husband to work.

336
23:24.647 --> 23:29.188
He had been working late every day.

337
23:29.188 --> 23:32.439
He fell asleep once he got on the car that day too.

338
23:32.439 --> 23:34.772
I just thought he must be tired.

339
23:38.105 --> 23:39.897
What's happening?

340
23:42.023 --> 23:45.388
No, no, why?

341
23:46.230 --> 23:48.647
What's happening? No, no!

342
23:48.647 --> 23:50.564
Honey!

343
23:56.647 --> 23:59.856
I hit the brake to the floor, but it didn't work.

344
24:00.397 --> 24:02.981
The steering wheel was out of control.

345
24:04.272 --> 24:06.305
When I realised what happened…

346
24:07.772 --> 24:12.472
Was your husband wearing the seatbelt?

347
24:13.230 --> 24:15.564
I don't know for sure, but…

348
24:15.564 --> 24:17.605
he should have been.

349
24:17.605 --> 24:22.023
Otherwise, the alarm goes off. But they didn't.

350
24:23.105 --> 24:25.731
I heard you trying to wake him up.

351
24:25.731 --> 24:28.731
But according to the dash cam clip, it seemed like he didn't wake up.

352
24:28.731 --> 24:31.223
Not even the slightest response.

353
24:31.731 --> 24:34.689
You're right. He slept through it.

354
24:34.689 --> 24:38.314
The passenger airbag didn't work.

355
24:38.314 --> 24:41.064
Did you disable it on purpose?

356
24:41.064 --> 24:42.230
Disabled?

357
24:42.230 --> 24:43.897
The airbag.

358
24:43.897 --> 24:47.014
Records say you don't have children.

359
24:48.064 --> 24:49.856
You're right.

360
24:49.856 --> 24:53.314
Except for the one I'm carrying here.

361
24:53.314 --> 24:55.731
Then why did you disable it?

362
24:55.731 --> 24:58.605
You need a mechanic to do that.

363
24:58.605 --> 25:00.564
I didn't even know you could do that.

364
25:00.564 --> 25:03.689
Your husband doesn't have a license. If you didn't disable it-

365
25:03.689 --> 25:06.223
I had no idea.

366
25:20.897 --> 25:22.772
Officers, I presume?

367
25:22.772 --> 25:26.223
I am her father.

368
25:31.605 --> 25:34.647
100% pressure on the gas right up until collision.

369
25:34.647 --> 25:37.272
No pressure detected on the brake.

370
25:37.272 --> 25:40.480
The driver did not use the brake.

371
25:40.480 --> 25:42.605
All control systems were normal.

372
25:42.605 --> 25:45.355
[ESC: Electronic Stability Control] No ESC or SCC error, either.

373
25:45.355 --> 25:48.105
[SCC: Smart Cruise Control] What are the chances for sudden acceleration?

374
25:48.105 --> 25:52.480
My money is on driver error, not sudden acceleration.

375
25:52.480 --> 25:55.023
There was no mechanical issue.

376
25:55.023 --> 25:57.897
However, some CAN data are missing,

377
25:57.897 --> 26:01.647
[CAN: Controller Area Network] at around 1.6 seconds before collision.

378
26:01.647 --> 26:03.230
It means…

379
26:03.230 --> 26:06.522
The car's system signals went dead for a second.

380
26:06.522 --> 26:09.023
Sensor power issue,

381
26:09.023 --> 26:11.272
electric interference…

382
26:11.272 --> 26:12.981
Anything could have caused it.

383
26:12.981 --> 26:14.355
Not a major issue, then?

384
26:14.355 --> 26:17.355
"Nothing significant to report" for now.

385
26:17.355 --> 26:19.647
-All right, thank you. -Thank you.

386
26:25.397 --> 26:28.564
- This car… - It came in a few days ago.

387
26:28.564 --> 26:30.230
A hit-and-run.

388
26:31.064 --> 26:32.522
With VIN damaged and

389
26:32.522 --> 26:35.230
the number plate missing, we can't identify the owner.

390
26:35.230 --> 26:37.731
We are checking for possible DNA.

391
26:37.731 --> 26:39.522
Have you had any luck?

392
26:39.522 --> 26:41.105
No.

393
26:44.230 --> 26:46.605
Still looking, are you?

394
26:48.230 --> 26:50.397
The driver who killed your wife.

395
26:55.605 --> 26:57.522
You met the judge?

396
26:57.522 --> 26:59.480
Yeah, it was so awkward.

397
26:59.480 --> 27:01.772
What did he say?

398
27:01.772 --> 27:04.647
"I have total faith in the forensic report.

399
27:04.647 --> 27:06.814
- However, - However,

400
27:06.814 --> 27:10.188
I didn't raise a senseless child.

401
27:10.188 --> 27:11.814
- Please leave all possibilities open - Please leave all possibilities open

402
27:11.814 --> 27:14.856
until you reach a concrete conclusion."

403
27:14.856 --> 27:16.564
He's a judge, all right.

404
27:16.564 --> 27:18.522
And his closing statement,

405
27:18.522 --> 27:21.897
"I'm a Supreme Court Justice, but you must not let that affect anything."

406
27:21.897 --> 27:25.064
Huh? So is he pressuring you or not?

407
27:25.064 --> 27:26.439
Exactly.

408
27:26.439 --> 27:29.897
"Don't think about the elephant," and you end up thinking about it.

409
27:29.897 --> 27:32.856
Elephant… that's difficult.

410
27:32.856 --> 27:34.355
Stop.

411
27:35.355 --> 27:38.731
I hear the superintendent's voice.

412
27:41.064 --> 27:43.064
What's going on?

413
27:43.064 --> 27:46.439
-Are they laughing? -This is a traffic investigation, right?

414
27:46.439 --> 27:49.564
This is no place for laughter.

415
28:03.314 --> 28:05.439
Who is that? A celebrity?

416
28:05.439 --> 28:07.439
The uniform looks good on him.

417
28:07.439 --> 28:09.439
Is he an idol?

418
28:09.439 --> 28:11.439
He must be filming something here.

419
28:11.439 --> 28:12.981
Let's go.

420
28:15.522 --> 28:17.230
Ma'am?

421
28:21.023 --> 28:23.314
He is our new trainee.

422
28:23.314 --> 28:27.023
It's the first day of the trainee rotation program.

423
28:27.897 --> 28:30.939
And we drew the long straw!

424
28:30.939 --> 28:33.147
You are weirdly happy. Aren't you pregnant?

425
28:33.147 --> 28:36.314
Can I not be happy just because I'm pregnant?

426
28:36.314 --> 28:38.230
After being stuck with you guys all this time,

427
28:38.230 --> 28:42.731
he's a sight to the sore eyes. The baby will love it, too.

428
28:42.731 --> 28:46.064
I'm so happy for you, little one.

429
28:46.064 --> 28:48.105
Dae Se, let me introduce you.

430
28:48.105 --> 28:50.689
They are your seniors from TCI.

431
28:50.689 --> 28:52.814
Wow, no way!

432
28:52.814 --> 28:55.355
Traffic Crimes Investigation, right?

433
28:55.355 --> 28:57.264
I saw the news last year.

434
28:58.064 --> 28:59.689
Salute!

435
28:59.689 --> 29:03.147
Central Police Academy, Class 317, Trainee Ji Dae Se, reporting!

436
29:03.147 --> 29:04.814
It's an honor to meet you!

437
29:04.814 --> 29:07.023
Honor, right…

438
29:07.023 --> 29:08.939
- Hi, I'm Min So Hee. - Glad to meet you.

439
29:08.939 --> 29:11.230
- Eo Hyun Kyung. - How do you do.

440
29:11.230 --> 29:14.230
Does the Traffic Division hire people by looks?

441
29:14.230 --> 29:16.897
Everyone is so good looking.

442
29:16.897 --> 29:18.772
I mean,

443
29:18.772 --> 29:20.314
look at our beautiful chief.

444
29:20.314 --> 29:22.397
What are you even saying?

445
29:22.397 --> 29:24.981
Come here, you!

446
29:24.981 --> 29:26.064
Wow!

447
29:26.064 --> 29:28.014
I'm older than I look.

448
29:31.023 --> 29:32.731
Excuse us, ma'am.

449
29:32.731 --> 29:34.439
Stay here for a few days.

450
29:34.439 --> 29:36.105
There are people watching.

451
29:36.105 --> 29:38.605
If you go home, it will rile them up.

452
29:38.605 --> 29:42.023
She needs to be at the funeral.

453
29:42.023 --> 29:44.480
And let her face the humiliation?

454
29:45.856 --> 29:49.181
You explain things to the in-laws.

455
29:49.939 --> 29:52.605
Can't you even drive?

456
29:53.647 --> 29:55.272
And you had run your mouth.

457
29:55.272 --> 29:56.480
I meant what I said.

458
29:56.480 --> 29:57.522
Who would believe you?

459
29:57.522 --> 29:58.647
I didn't lie!

460
29:58.647 --> 30:00.939
- I have never- - Darling.

461
30:00.939 --> 30:02.680
Please.

462
30:05.564 --> 30:07.889
What are you worried about?

463
30:08.439 --> 30:10.889
Me, or your reputation?

464
30:11.397 --> 30:13.605
Or the company?

465
30:13.605 --> 30:16.931
Are you worried this will affect the company?

466
30:23.355 --> 30:26.397
All case records are here.

467
30:26.397 --> 30:29.023
If you have questions, ask the captain.

468
30:29.023 --> 30:32.480
- The evidence room is… - He's so green! I was once like that.

469
30:32.480 --> 30:34.856
Are you for real? Just look at that photo.

470
30:34.856 --> 30:38.647
That photo betrayed me!

471
30:38.647 --> 30:41.397
Inspector Cha, you seen this? He looks like a high schooler!

472
30:41.397 --> 30:43.897
- He's hitting me, Captain! - I didn't!

473
30:43.897 --> 30:46.772
- I had a late night snack. - Captain!

474
30:46.772 --> 30:47.981
- That's why I look so big. - Whatever.

475
30:47.981 --> 30:50.147
Dong Gi! Let's start the meeting.

476
30:50.147 --> 30:52.064
- Sorry, sir. - Okay.

477
30:52.064 --> 30:54.480
- The wrinkles… - Right?

478
30:54.480 --> 30:57.772
Captain? He wants to sit in our meeting.

479
30:57.772 --> 30:59.689
I'll just watch.

480
31:00.397 --> 31:01.689
Take a seat.

481
31:01.689 --> 31:03.188
Just watch.

482
31:03.188 --> 31:05.689
Don't listen.

483
31:05.689 --> 31:07.314
You laughed? Is this a joke to you?

484
31:07.314 --> 31:09.397
- Sorry, sir. - Dong Gi.

485
31:09.397 --> 31:11.105
Come.

486
31:13.605 --> 31:15.939
How was the meeting with Han Soo In?

487
31:15.939 --> 31:18.230
She is sticking with sudden acceleration.

488
31:18.230 --> 31:21.814
Says the husband didn't wake up, she thinks it's strange too.

489
31:21.814 --> 31:24.605
-The airbag? -She said she did not disable it.

490
31:24.605 --> 31:25.814
Except for the baby in her tummy,

491
31:25.814 --> 31:27.897
there were no children.

492
31:27.897 --> 31:31.439
I don't think she was lying when she said she didn't know how to disable it..

493
31:31.439 --> 31:36.264
Many drivers don't know much about their cars.

494
31:37.230 --> 31:40.564
I met her father, the judge.

495
31:40.564 --> 31:42.647
He told me to ignore his position.

496
31:42.647 --> 31:44.856
No way! It's that case, right?

497
31:44.856 --> 31:47.639
The one where the judge's daughter claims sudden acceleration! Right?

498
31:48.480 --> 31:51.439
Seriously… who said you could speak?

499
31:51.439 --> 31:53.147
I said just watch!

500
31:53.147 --> 31:55.188
I'm sorry.

501
31:55.188 --> 31:57.564
How about the people close to her?

502
31:57.564 --> 31:58.689
Before we get to that,

503
31:58.689 --> 32:01.772
let me show you the insurance records.

504
32:01.772 --> 32:04.981
Like I expected, there are policies covering the husband, Baek Sung Min.

505
32:04.981 --> 32:07.772
Two life insurance, worth 1.2 billion won.

506
32:07.772 --> 32:09.514
The beneficiary is

507
32:10.105 --> 32:11.147
Han Soo In of course.

508
32:11.147 --> 32:13.814
- When did they sign up? - Around three years ago.

509
32:13.814 --> 32:14.939
That's quite long ago.

510
32:14.939 --> 32:17.605
But four months ago, a rider was added.

511
32:17.605 --> 32:19.897
If he dies by an accident, including traffic accidents,

512
32:19.897 --> 32:22.314
the insurance money doubles.

513
32:22.314 --> 32:23.397
2.4 billion in total.

514
32:23.397 --> 32:26.397
Wow, this is insane.

515
32:30.981 --> 32:35.897
But why would she want the money?

516
32:35.897 --> 32:38.647
Right. Her father is a judge.

517
32:38.647 --> 32:40.564
Does she need to kill her husband for money?

518
32:40.564 --> 32:44.439
She looks wealthy only on the surface.

519
32:44.439 --> 32:47.605
I asked around, and she is a big spender.

520
32:47.605 --> 32:50.939
As you can see here.

521
32:50.939 --> 32:53.772
Golf, travel, what not.

522
32:53.772 --> 32:57.230
She's constantly juggling credit cards.

523
32:57.230 --> 33:00.355
Her mother supported her for a while,

524
33:00.355 --> 33:03.605
until her father found out and put a stop to it.

525
33:03.605 --> 33:06.480
The father's not looking good, either.

526
33:06.480 --> 33:08.522
He invested all his assets in a startup,

527
33:08.522 --> 33:10.188
which is not doing very well.

528
33:10.188 --> 33:12.731
He has got nothing except the apartment house.

529
33:12.731 --> 33:18.314
Han Soo In's husband happens to be a researcher at the company.

530
33:19.188 --> 33:22.639
Chimera, Dreaming the Future of Mobility.

531
33:25.772 --> 33:28.355
Develops simulation platforms,

532
33:28.355 --> 33:30.514
and researches self-driving techs.

533
33:34.105 --> 33:36.139
What about the forensic results?

534
33:39.897 --> 33:41.439
Just as expected.

535
33:42.230 --> 33:44.522
No brake pressure,

536
33:44.522 --> 33:46.731
full gas before the accident,

537
33:46.731 --> 33:48.731
and no mechanical issue.

538
33:48.731 --> 33:50.731
Driver error, highly likely.

539
33:50.731 --> 33:52.856
See? I told you it's obvious!

540
33:52.856 --> 33:55.480
- If that's the case- - We have two possibilities.

541
33:55.480 --> 33:58.347
Accidental, or intentional.

542
34:06.314 --> 34:10.230
[Driver: Han Soo In , Passenger: Baek Sung Min Victim: Lee Do Hyun]

543
34:10.230 --> 34:12.772
[Taxi license: Ahn Yong Geon]

544
34:12.772 --> 34:14.564
[Owner-Driver Taxi]

545
34:14.564 --> 34:16.355
[Taxi license: Choi Seung Hun]

546
34:19.188 --> 34:21.064
[Taxi license: Ahn Yong Geon]

547
34:25.439 --> 34:28.731
I raised So Hee all these years

548
34:28.731 --> 34:31.314
- with the help of this one. - Yong Geon.

549
34:31.314 --> 34:33.064
Hate to part with it, huh?

550
34:33.064 --> 34:35.689
I would give him mine,

551
34:35.689 --> 34:38.223
but I still need this job.

552
34:38.897 --> 34:42.314
But I don't feel so sad

553
34:42.314 --> 34:44.772
knowing your son will drive it.

554
34:44.772 --> 34:46.397
-Seung Hun? -Yes?

555
34:46.397 --> 34:49.564
Take care of her for me.

556
34:49.564 --> 34:51.647
And make lots of money.

557
34:51.647 --> 34:55.314
He lowered the price for you. Be nice to him.

558
34:55.314 --> 34:57.939
- Think of him as your father. - No need for that.

559
34:57.939 --> 35:00.772
I really appreciate it.

560
35:00.772 --> 35:02.897
Let's meet often.

561
35:02.897 --> 35:05.223
- Drive safe. - I will.

562
35:07.105 --> 35:08.856
Congrats on your new journey.

563
35:08.856 --> 35:10.105
I will drop by soon.

564
35:10.105 --> 35:11.564
Let's grab a drink.

565
35:11.564 --> 35:13.355
Anytime.

566
35:13.355 --> 35:14.889
Now,

567
35:15.772 --> 35:17.856
here you go.

568
35:17.856 --> 35:20.181
-Thank you. -Sure.

569
35:32.439 --> 35:34.897
[So Hee's Diner]

570
35:42.230 --> 35:44.397
What do you mean, autopsy?

571
35:44.397 --> 35:46.147
- But why? - We would like to know,

572
35:46.147 --> 35:49.105
about Mr. Baek's health conditions.

573
35:49.105 --> 35:52.772
We need to identify the cause before the cremation.

574
35:52.772 --> 35:56.522
What are you trying to find out?

575
35:56.522 --> 36:00.188
What? Is it homicide?

576
36:00.188 --> 36:02.772
It is still too early too-

577
36:02.772 --> 36:05.397
I knew something was off.

578
36:05.397 --> 36:07.939
Why was his airbag the only one disabled?

579
36:07.939 --> 36:10.064
She is barely injured!

580
36:10.064 --> 36:11.397
Like I said before,

581
36:11.397 --> 36:14.347
they shouldn't have got married.

582
36:16.272 --> 36:17.981
What do you mean?

583
36:17.981 --> 36:19.647
Why shouldn't they have?

584
36:19.647 --> 36:21.555
It was an arranged marriage,

585
36:22.272 --> 36:24.147
from the very beginning.

586
36:24.147 --> 36:27.731
He arranged the marriage.

587
36:27.731 --> 36:29.064
That famous judge.

588
36:29.064 --> 36:30.397
Dr. Baek.

589
36:30.397 --> 36:32.564
When he was developing

590
36:32.564 --> 36:34.897
the algorithm or some patent,

591
36:34.897 --> 36:37.856
the father-in-law offered to invest.

592
36:38.605 --> 36:41.772
He planned to take my brother under his wing,

593
36:41.772 --> 36:44.722
and take my brother's share of the patent for himself.

594
36:47.856 --> 36:52.897
If Baek Sung Min is found to have been killed by accident or sudden acceleration,

595
36:52.897 --> 36:55.605
his share will go to his next of kin, Han Soo In.

596
36:55.605 --> 36:59.023
Justice Han will have more control over Chimera.

597
36:59.023 --> 37:03.480
He gets the share and the money

598
37:03.480 --> 37:06.564
if no foul play is found.

599
37:06.564 --> 37:08.355
Hold on.

600
37:08.355 --> 37:09.981
- Hi, Dad. - Are you busy?

601
37:09.981 --> 37:11.939
No, it's okay.

602
37:11.939 --> 37:14.981
I…

603
37:15.772 --> 37:17.772
handed over the taxi.

604
37:17.772 --> 37:20.272
Gang Won and his son came,

605
37:20.272 --> 37:23.555
and took over the taxi.

606
37:24.605 --> 37:27.064
You did?

607
37:27.064 --> 37:28.680
You must be…

608
37:29.314 --> 37:31.889
- feeling sad. - Sad?

609
37:33.981 --> 37:36.188
It's a burden off my shoulders.

610
37:36.188 --> 37:38.355
Right. I know you worked so hard.

611
37:38.355 --> 37:39.564
See you at home.

612
37:39.564 --> 37:41.514
Okay.

613
37:44.522 --> 37:47.647
Did he sell the taxi?

614
37:47.647 --> 37:49.689
Yes.

615
37:49.689 --> 37:52.689
He says he's fine but,

616
37:52.689 --> 37:54.764
he didn't sound like it.

617
37:56.480 --> 38:00.188
I wonder what it feels like to quit a job

618
38:00.188 --> 38:01.897
you worked at for 30 years.

619
38:04.064 --> 38:06.897
Well, I guess…

620
38:09.689 --> 38:13.847
he will miss the rumbling when the engine starts and turns off.

621
38:15.605 --> 38:19.931
I used to fall asleep hearing that rumbling.

622
38:21.272 --> 38:25.264
He must feel twice as lost without it.

623
38:32.605 --> 38:36.147
Chimera does not just make self-driving tech.

624
38:36.147 --> 38:38.439
It develops thinking machines.

625
38:38.439 --> 38:41.605
What was Dr. Baek's job here?

626
38:41.605 --> 38:45.897
He designed ways to assess threats to people, things, and animals,

627
38:45.897 --> 38:48.605
and determine which to avoid first.

628
38:48.605 --> 38:50.814
You mean, which ones to avoid,

629
38:50.814 --> 38:54.064
and which ones to hit first?

630
38:54.064 --> 38:57.814
Well, to be more precise,

631
38:57.814 --> 39:01.355
he designed the logic for the car's assessment.

632
39:01.355 --> 39:05.014
The algorithm makes the final decision, though.

633
39:06.064 --> 39:11.480
He always tried to approach it from humans' perspective.

634
39:11.480 --> 39:14.105
Beyond simply copying a human,

635
39:14.105 --> 39:19.064
he wanted the machine to think, take caution, and evade like humans do.

636
39:20.439 --> 39:23.355
He focused on avoiding accidents,

637
39:23.355 --> 39:26.856
and saving humans first.

638
39:29.188 --> 39:31.147
Losing Dr. Baek's will,

639
39:31.147 --> 39:33.931
is a big lost to the company.

640
39:34.439 --> 39:36.056
Yeon Ho?

641
39:37.439 --> 39:40.564
Palindrome? You are Palindrome, right?

642
39:40.564 --> 39:42.105
You still remember.

643
39:42.105 --> 39:43.689
My nickname.

644
39:50.105 --> 39:53.772
What was it back there? What drome?

645
39:53.772 --> 39:55.605
Palindrome.

646
39:55.605 --> 39:58.230
A word that sounds the same when read backwards.

647
39:58.230 --> 40:00.347
It's called a palindrome.

648
40:01.105 --> 40:04.188
Kayak, deed, rotator, noon, and Yoon-Ji-Yoon.

649
40:04.188 --> 40:06.397
My name is Yoon Ji Yoon.

650
40:06.397 --> 40:10.647
Oh, like Woo-Young-Woo! And Lee Hyo-Ii.

651
40:10.647 --> 40:12.480
- Like that? - That's right.

652
40:12.480 --> 40:16.605
Yeon Ho called me that in college.

653
40:16.605 --> 40:21.181
So you went to the same college?

654
40:37.314 --> 40:39.480
I still can't believe

655
40:39.480 --> 40:42.105
what happened to Dr. Baek.

656
40:42.105 --> 40:43.480
Were you two close?

657
40:43.480 --> 40:45.939
We did some projects together.

658
40:45.939 --> 40:48.805
Including the early version of this project.

659
40:49.897 --> 40:54.023
What was he like at work?

660
40:54.023 --> 40:56.264
Were there any problems?

661
40:59.314 --> 41:03.689
There were some conflicts recently.

662
41:03.689 --> 41:06.105
What do you mean?

663
41:06.105 --> 41:09.355
They had a big argument during a meeting.

664
41:09.355 --> 41:11.772
People's lives are at stake!

665
41:11.772 --> 41:13.897
You can't just wish problems away!

666
41:13.897 --> 41:17.564
That's gambling, not science!

667
41:17.564 --> 41:19.097
Sung Min.

668
41:20.147 --> 41:21.564
I didn't peg you as a coward.

669
41:21.564 --> 41:22.731
Geun Won…

670
41:22.731 --> 41:24.981
Mr. Cho and Dr. Baek,

671
41:24.981 --> 41:27.856
they clashed over AI ethics.

672
41:27.856 --> 41:30.147
Then Mr. Cho threatened a lawsuit.

673
41:30.147 --> 41:34.272
He talked about a patent lawsuit, things like that.

674
41:34.272 --> 41:39.347
So Dr. Baek was a threat to the company.

675
41:40.981 --> 41:42.847
Dr. Baek believed that

676
41:43.355 --> 41:46.397
technology can save humanity.

677
41:46.397 --> 41:50.772
Above all, he was committed to safety.

678
41:50.772 --> 41:52.814
That's why he took his time,

679
41:53.397 --> 41:58.056
which may have made some people uncomfortable.

680
42:06.522 --> 42:09.314
Look at all the flowers.

681
42:09.939 --> 42:12.097
I'm starving.

682
42:13.772 --> 42:15.897
Hey!

683
42:15.897 --> 42:17.105
The Chief is here!

684
42:17.105 --> 42:19.397
- Congratulations. - Thank you.

685
42:19.397 --> 42:21.147
Oh, thank you.

686
42:21.147 --> 42:23.397
This way.

687
42:23.397 --> 42:25.480
It's packed with people!

688
42:25.480 --> 42:26.647
You'll be rich soon.

689
42:26.647 --> 42:30.064
It's just the opening bloom.

690
42:30.064 --> 42:32.147
- I'll be right back. - Do what you need to.

691
42:32.147 --> 42:34.023
Thank you.

692
42:37.981 --> 42:40.397
Are they from the Traffic Division?

693
42:40.397 --> 42:42.564
What are they so excited about?

694
42:43.105 --> 42:44.480
Huh?

695
42:45.147 --> 42:48.064
Oh, he's the one!

696
42:48.064 --> 42:50.605
Ji Dae Se. Or was it Se Dae?

697
42:50.605 --> 42:53.522
The new pretty boy.

698
42:53.522 --> 42:57.689
Our female officers were fangirling over him, too.

699
42:57.689 --> 43:01.147
You call that good looking? He looks like a girl.

700
43:01.147 --> 43:04.397
I was a proper heartthrob when I was his age.

701
43:05.814 --> 43:07.397
Wow, that's funny.

702
43:07.397 --> 43:09.064
That was a good one.

703
43:09.064 --> 43:11.230
It was not a joke.

704
43:11.230 --> 43:13.772
What are you having? Pork cutlet for me.

705
43:13.772 --> 43:15.355
Dad!

706
43:15.355 --> 43:17.439
- You're here! - Hello.

707
43:17.439 --> 43:19.981
- Hello. - My, my.

708
43:20.856 --> 43:22.064
- Min So Hee! - Yes?

709
43:22.064 --> 43:25.230
- Congratulations! - I… thank you.

710
43:25.230 --> 43:27.522
It's embarrassing to see my name on the sign.

711
43:27.522 --> 43:30.439
No, it's heartwarming.

712
43:30.439 --> 43:32.314
People who heard of you

713
43:32.314 --> 43:36.939
will definitely want to come here.

714
43:36.939 --> 43:39.856
- Enjoy your meal. - You too.

715
43:39.856 --> 43:43.023
- Enjoy your meal. - Wait a minute.

716
43:43.023 --> 43:46.230
What about the former owner?

717
43:46.230 --> 43:48.647
Her daughter opened a Korean restaurant in New York.

718
43:48.647 --> 43:49.814
She is helping her there.

719
43:49.814 --> 43:50.939
She got a new job.

720
43:50.939 --> 43:54.355
Why, Korean food is really going global.

721
43:54.355 --> 43:56.647
K-wave is really a thing.

722
43:56.647 --> 43:59.314
She was such a nice owner.

723
43:59.314 --> 44:03.897
She was so lovely, and her food was great.

724
44:03.897 --> 44:08.097
It was excellent.

725
44:08.897 --> 44:10.314
Enjoy the food.

726
44:10.314 --> 44:12.722
- Bon apetit. - Have a nice meal.

727
44:13.689 --> 44:15.388
Did you hear?

728
44:15.939 --> 44:18.522
About the former owner?

729
44:18.522 --> 44:21.847
Chief tried hitting on her.

730
44:22.897 --> 44:26.105
What are you doing?

731
44:26.105 --> 44:27.647
I like you.

732
44:27.647 --> 44:29.181
What?

733
44:30.023 --> 44:31.564
Wh-what did you say?

734
44:31.564 --> 44:33.397
Did you just confess?

735
44:33.397 --> 44:35.355
Good heavens.

736
44:35.355 --> 44:36.355
This isn't right.

737
44:36.355 --> 44:38.147
Oh my goodness.

738
44:38.147 --> 44:40.897
Why are your eyes so sad?

739
44:40.897 --> 44:42.605
Confess? Confess what?

740
44:42.605 --> 44:44.314
Chief got so drunk,

741
44:44.314 --> 44:47.314
he grabbed her hands and said she reminds him of his first love.

742
44:47.314 --> 44:50.564
- Yucks! - That's just pathetic!

743
44:50.564 --> 44:52.147
No wonder he got divorced.

744
44:52.147 --> 44:55.564
Talk about ageing badly. First love? Give me a break.

745
44:55.564 --> 44:56.689
Yuck.

746
44:56.689 --> 44:59.105
Stop being so nosy.

747
44:59.105 --> 45:00.731
Let's just eat bulgogi.

748
45:00.731 --> 45:02.188
New owner. It's not bulgogi.

749
45:02.188 --> 45:04.314
- Right. Jeyuk. - Jeyuk.

750
45:27.314 --> 45:29.480
Steering angle log.

751
45:29.480 --> 45:31.439
[Time / Steering Angle]

752
45:31.439 --> 45:36.856
2.8 to 12.3 in 0.3 seconds?

753
45:42.731 --> 45:44.264
Honey!

754
45:51.939 --> 45:55.064
I hit the brake to the floor, but it didn't work.

755
45:55.064 --> 45:57.772
The steering wheel was out of control.

756
45:59.647 --> 46:02.439
The car went out of control.

757
46:02.439 --> 46:04.605
The car…

758
46:04.605 --> 46:07.355
was controlled by someone?

759
46:08.981 --> 46:10.647
I knew it.

760
46:11.188 --> 46:13.272
- Have you eaten? - No.

761
46:13.272 --> 46:17.105
Don't skip your meal. Otherwise, what's the point?

762
46:17.105 --> 46:19.147
My father's side dishes and kimchi.

763
46:19.147 --> 46:21.772
- Mix them up and- - Let's go.

764
46:21.772 --> 46:24.689
Go where? You need to eat.

765
46:24.689 --> 46:26.522
Come and find out.

766
46:26.522 --> 46:28.188
Eat first, then go.

767
46:29.064 --> 46:30.597
Let's go now.

768
46:40.564 --> 46:42.981
Sorry, I know it's late.

769
46:42.981 --> 46:44.647
Save it for later.

770
46:53.480 --> 46:56.605
[TCU: Transmission Control Unit] These are TCU and ADAS ESCU logs, right?

771
46:56.605 --> 46:59.564
[ADAS ECU: Advanced Driver Assistance Systems] They match the case records.

772
46:59.564 --> 47:03.480
That's weird. These are not typical driving patterns.

773
47:03.480 --> 47:07.105
A conditional execution routine is hidden here.

774
47:09.355 --> 47:11.305
Someone wrote it in.

775
47:12.897 --> 47:14.480
What do you mean?

776
47:14.480 --> 47:16.564
You mean the car didn't malfunction?

777
47:16.564 --> 47:18.355
Someone planned it?

778
47:18.355 --> 47:22.314
Here. The condition includes a GPS coordinate.

779
47:22.314 --> 47:25.355
Road ID: D894X.

780
47:25.355 --> 47:27.105
Where is it?

781
47:27.105 --> 47:28.680
Hold on a sec.

782
47:29.188 --> 47:32.105
Naeguro 20-gil, Bunjeong-gu, Seonghan-si, Gyeonggi-do.

783
47:32.105 --> 47:33.522
That's where the car crashed.

784
47:33.522 --> 47:35.522
Was it the trigger?

785
47:35.522 --> 47:37.731
One more thing.

786
47:37.731 --> 47:40.397
Here, "passenger seat occupied."

787
47:40.397 --> 47:43.105
There must be a passenger.

788
47:43.105 --> 47:44.897
If the two conditions are met,

789
47:44.897 --> 47:46.981
the hidden command is executed.

790
47:46.981 --> 47:49.522
The car accelerates,

791
47:49.522 --> 47:51.522
steering fixed at 12.3 degrees,

792
47:51.522 --> 47:54.480
and the brake don't work.

793
47:54.480 --> 47:58.981
What do you mean? When the car reaches this road,

794
47:58.981 --> 48:00.814
it starts to move on its own?

795
48:00.814 --> 48:03.230
Dr. Baek was the target.

796
48:03.230 --> 48:05.772
He was a dead man

797
48:05.772 --> 48:08.056
the moment he got in the car.

798
48:09.731 --> 48:13.397
It was not an accident. It was a murder by design.

799
48:15.689 --> 48:19.731
Someone hacked a car to kill?

800
48:19.731 --> 48:21.856
Who would do such a…

801
48:22.731 --> 48:24.347
Mr. Cho.

802
48:24.856 --> 48:26.188
As long-time partners,

803
48:26.188 --> 48:29.023
he and Dr. Baek developed the system together.

804
48:36.147 --> 48:37.480
A murder?

805
48:37.480 --> 48:41.605
A murder disguised as driver error or malfunction.

806
48:42.272 --> 48:43.897
Come to think of it, when I went to NFS,

807
48:43.897 --> 48:46.147
Researcher Kang told me something.

808
48:46.147 --> 48:49.605
Some data were missing right before the collision.

809
48:49.605 --> 48:51.897
[CAN: Controller Area Network] CAN data.

810
48:51.897 --> 48:55.355
- Yeah, that. - CAN data? What's that?

811
48:55.355 --> 48:58.647
In the car's internal network,

812
48:58.647 --> 49:01.314
some data were removed or not recorded on purpose.

813
49:01.314 --> 49:05.397
The missing section must be when the command was executed.

814
49:05.397 --> 49:08.314
The culprit is working for Chimera, then!

815
49:12.230 --> 49:15.272
How long have you been there?

816
49:15.272 --> 49:18.355
- Since a while ago. - I called him.

817
49:18.355 --> 49:21.023
Superintendent wants us to take him in.

818
49:21.023 --> 49:24.064
Why? What are we, babysitters?

819
49:24.064 --> 49:25.856
Who knows?

820
49:25.856 --> 49:27.522
Like they say, a good smith can shape any iron.

821
49:27.522 --> 49:30.064
With polishing, he might become our greatest asset.

822
49:30.064 --> 49:32.772
I'll make a great blacksmith, sir!

823
49:32.772 --> 49:34.147
That's not what I meant.

824
49:34.147 --> 49:38.064
Okay. I can't promise you anything, but come here and observe.

825
49:38.064 --> 49:39.647
Thank you, ma'am!

826
49:41.981 --> 49:44.023
Raise your hand first before you say something.

827
49:44.023 --> 49:46.064
- Okay? - Yes, sir!

828
49:46.064 --> 49:47.897
Just like that.

829
49:47.897 --> 49:50.439
Such a crime can be committed

830
49:50.439 --> 49:52.689
only by someone working for Chimera.

831
49:52.689 --> 49:55.064
That's right, considering the MO.

832
49:55.064 --> 49:58.480
Someone related to that company. where Baek Sung Min used to work?

833
49:58.480 --> 50:03.397
You're on the right track. So, our focus is on this guy.

834
50:03.397 --> 50:05.981
Cho Geun Won, CEO of Chimera.

835
50:05.981 --> 50:09.397
He frequently clashed with Baek Sung Min over the company's IPO.

836
50:09.397 --> 50:13.564
He's one of the few people with the knowledge to do this.

837
50:13.564 --> 50:15.814
Cho Geun Won. Double check.

838
50:24.147 --> 50:26.397
Can I help you?

839
50:26.397 --> 50:29.639
- My name is Cho Geun Won. - Nice to meet you.

840
50:30.397 --> 50:32.347
Cho Geun Won?

841
50:33.272 --> 50:35.188
- Cho Geun Won! - Yes, Mr. Cho!

842
50:35.188 --> 50:36.814
May I ask what you're doing here?

843
50:36.814 --> 50:38.897
Hi. Sorry for the interruption.

844
50:38.897 --> 50:41.230
I have something to give you.

845
50:41.230 --> 50:42.897
Oh.

846
50:42.897 --> 50:46.731
- We're having a meeting. This way. - Apologies.

847
50:46.731 --> 50:48.472
Take care.

848
50:50.647 --> 50:52.188
This way.

849
50:57.230 --> 50:58.605
Wow.

850
51:03.564 --> 51:07.731
Something came up during a security check.

851
51:08.939 --> 51:09.981
What…

852
51:09.981 --> 51:15.981
Someone accessed Ms. Han's car from one of our computers.

853
51:15.981 --> 51:20.772
It was not a simple diagnosis. I found an auto execution protocol.

854
51:20.772 --> 51:25.347
It can fix the car's speed, disable the brake, and control steering.

855
51:26.564 --> 51:32.647
I think someone staged the accident,

856
51:32.647 --> 51:34.647
to take Dr. Baek's life.

857
51:35.230 --> 51:38.355
Do you know who accessed it?

858
51:40.939 --> 51:43.056
I checked the account.

859
51:43.939 --> 51:46.555
It belonged to Yoon Ji Yoon.

860
51:47.480 --> 51:50.981
Unfortunately, security camera clips have been erased.

861
51:50.981 --> 51:53.272
- Erased? - Yes.

862
51:53.272 --> 51:54.981
I found the access log,

863
51:54.981 --> 51:58.064
but camera recordings around that time are gone.

864
51:58.064 --> 52:01.722
So, I copied all available files.

865
52:05.397 --> 52:08.814
We'll take a look at it.

866
52:08.814 --> 52:11.897
I'm not sure it's appropriate,

867
52:11.897 --> 52:13.856
but there were rumors

868
52:13.856 --> 52:18.647
that Yoon Ji Yoon and Dr. Baek,

869
52:18.647 --> 52:20.230
were lovers.

870
52:20.772 --> 52:23.772
But they seem to have fell out recently.

871
52:23.772 --> 52:26.272
More recently, Dr. Baek

872
52:26.272 --> 52:29.223
removed Yoon Ji Yoon from his project.

873
52:36.439 --> 52:38.272
Log files,

874
52:39.355 --> 52:41.722
access time,

875
52:45.147 --> 52:48.230
command structure. There are no signs of tampering.

876
52:48.230 --> 52:51.314
It was her account, then?

877
52:51.314 --> 52:53.023
Technically, yes.

878
52:53.023 --> 52:56.480
She has a motive, if what Mr. Cho said is true.

879
52:56.480 --> 53:00.272
If she was kicked from the project and her relationship went sour,

880
53:00.272 --> 53:03.480
she lost both her position and lover.

881
53:03.480 --> 53:06.314
Does that make sense? Her, of all people?

882
53:06.314 --> 53:08.981
-Who's Yoon Ji Yoon, anyway? -Do we know her?

883
53:08.981 --> 53:12.314
Inspector Cha's college friend. Palindrome.

884
53:12.314 --> 53:13.605
What drome?

885
53:13.605 --> 53:15.105
It can be someone else.

886
53:15.105 --> 53:18.397
Employees have easy access to their coworkers' terminals.

887
53:18.397 --> 53:22.230
That's possible. However, Ji Yoon had an admin account.

888
53:22.230 --> 53:24.314
To access the account, the user needs to know the ID,

889
53:24.314 --> 53:28.023
access a set computer, and pass the authenticator.

890
53:28.023 --> 53:29.981
Okay, I get the situation.

891
53:29.981 --> 53:33.514
But do you also think that Yoon Ji Yoon is responsible?

892
53:34.522 --> 53:37.931
We have to find out.

893
53:51.647 --> 53:53.939
[SIM log / IPO data. Driving test results]

894
54:18.689 --> 54:21.272
Yeon Ho? What are you doing here?

895
54:21.272 --> 54:22.772
We need to talk.

896
54:22.772 --> 54:24.355
Me too.

897
54:25.105 --> 54:27.397
Get in. We'll talk in the car.

898
54:27.397 --> 54:29.064
Okay.

899
54:29.064 --> 54:31.522
You seem to be in a hurry.

900
54:32.314 --> 54:35.731
- What did you want to talk about? - You go first.

901
54:35.731 --> 54:37.230
You first.

902
54:38.564 --> 54:41.188
What is your relationship with Dr. Baek?

903
54:41.188 --> 54:43.522
They say you had an affair with him,

904
54:43.522 --> 54:46.647
but you were removed from the project,

905
54:46.647 --> 54:49.147
along with your access to key codes.

906
54:49.147 --> 54:50.272
That's-

907
54:50.272 --> 54:52.314
Is that why you did it?

908
54:52.314 --> 54:54.230
Because he betrayed you?

909
54:54.230 --> 54:56.439
Or did you kill him

910
54:56.439 --> 54:58.472
so you can take his place?

911
55:02.397 --> 55:05.647
Oh my. I'm sorry.

912
55:05.647 --> 55:08.731
I don't know what got into me.

913
55:08.731 --> 55:10.305
You better drive.

914
55:23.480 --> 55:27.105
Dr. Baek couldn't deal with the fact that his project

915
55:27.105 --> 55:31.230
became a chessboard for capital and power play.

916
55:31.230 --> 55:33.480
Mr. Cho and Justice Han gave him so much pressure,

917
55:33.480 --> 55:37.814
and threatened to kick Dr. Baek from his own project.

918
55:37.814 --> 55:39.064
In that case,

919
55:39.064 --> 55:41.939
someone had to see the project through to the end.

920
55:41.939 --> 55:45.522
That's why he removed me from the project,

921
55:45.522 --> 55:48.647
to take all the responsibilities.

922
55:48.647 --> 55:51.605
We found records of someone hacking into Ms. Han's car.

923
55:51.605 --> 55:55.522
Your account ran the protocol. I need explanation.

924
55:55.522 --> 55:59.439
Cho Geun Won did it. I just found out today.

925
55:59.439 --> 56:04.097
I also found out what he did to get the IPO going.

926
56:08.188 --> 56:10.272
To get better performance,

927
56:10.272 --> 56:14.230
Mr. Cho was using a risky logic in real world driving tests.

928
56:14.230 --> 56:18.522
It ignores sensors and fixes response times

929
56:18.522 --> 56:22.889
to make it look like self-driving is working.

930
56:23.647 --> 56:26.105
Can you prove that?

931
56:26.105 --> 56:28.139
The evidence is in that bag.

932
56:41.314 --> 56:44.188
- What is it? - The brake feels off.

933
56:44.188 --> 56:45.397
Are you pressing the gas?

934
56:45.397 --> 56:48.023
No, but the car is…

935
56:48.023 --> 56:49.605
The brake!

936
56:49.605 --> 56:51.564
The brake is acting weird!

937
56:57.439 --> 57:00.147
Hit a wall! Slow the car down!

938
57:36.689 --> 57:38.314
Cell runaway imminent evacuate now.

939
57:38.314 --> 57:39.814
Get out.

940
57:40.605 --> 57:42.605
The door won't open!

941
57:49.023 --> 57:50.939
Come on, come on!

942
57:50.939 --> 57:52.814
The bag!

943
57:54.772 --> 57:56.522
Hurry!

944
59:04.814 --> 59:06.981
The only one capable of committing this crime is…

945
59:06.981 --> 59:08.564
Baek Sung Min is already dead.

946
59:08.564 --> 59:09.856
He's the victim.

947
59:09.856 --> 59:12.188
Are you saying Han Soo In could have murdered him?

948
59:12.188 --> 59:14.105
Let's find out.

949
59:14.105 --> 59:15.731
It's not over.

950
59:21.647 --> 59:23.439
Why did you suddenly take your clothes off?

951
59:23.439 --> 59:25.814
Train as if it's real.

952
59:25.814 --> 59:27.480
I have to be somewhere.

953
59:27.480 --> 59:29.605
The brake isn't working.
